{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneFiveFoldStructure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneFiveFoldStructure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S5SO3FiberAction"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.image_card_four_plus_T2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.image_card_four_plus_T2","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneFiveFoldStructure.lean#L64-L70","doc":"**Four partition-image irreps + one chirality completion.** The image of `toA5Irrep` over the\nseven partitions has exactly four elements `{A, T₁, G, H}`; adjoining the missing chirality partner\n`T₂` (from the electron block) completes the five. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.five_fold_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.five_fold_count","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneFiveFoldStructure.lean#L60-L62","doc":"**The five-fold count `1 + 1 + 1 + 2 = 5`.** Three conjugate-pair irreps (`A`, `G`, `H`) plus the\nelectron-block chirality pair (`T₁ ⊕ T₂`) exhaust the five A₅ irreps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.toA5Irrep_eq_T1_iff_threeOneOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.toA5Irrep_eq_T1_iff_threeOneOne","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneFiveFoldStructure.lean#L54-L58","doc":"**`T₁` is reached only by the self-conjugate `(3,1,1)`.** The three conjugate *pairs* land on\n`A`, `G`, `H`; `T₁` (and its chirality partner `T₂`) come exclusively from the electron block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.toA5Irrep_ne_T2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.toA5Irrep_ne_T2","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneFiveFoldStructure.lean#L48-L52","doc":"**`toA5Irrep` misses `T₂`.** The partition→A₅-irrep restriction hits only four of the five irreps\n(`{A, T₁, G, H}`); `T₂` is absent — it is the chirality partner of `T₁`, supplied only by the\nself-conjugate `(3,1,1)` electron block's split `T₁ ⊕ T₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.self_conjugate_iff_threeOneOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.self_conjugate_iff_threeOneOne","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneFiveFoldStructure.lean#L42-L46","doc":"**The unique self-conjugate partition of 5 is `(3,1,1)`** — the electron block. Every other\npartition of 5 is paired with a distinct conjugate. ","signatureChunk":0}]}